+## 5. Phase 3 (KAN-413) Credential & Container Checklist
+
+Phase 3 executes live workouts on isolated local TLS staging without destructive mutations on `k.hackedyour.info`. The following prerequisites and credentials must be prepared:
+
+### 5.1 Cloud & Local AI Credentials
+1. **Google Gemini API Key:**
+   - Valid key with access to `gemini-2.5-flash` or `gemini-1.5-flash`.
+   - Used for live provider registration, model probing, and completion testing.
+2. **OpenAI API Key (or vLLM / LiteLLM Proxy):**
+   - Valid key or local OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
+   - Used for failover priority stack validation.
+3. **Local Ollama Runtime:**
+   - Active Ollama daemon listening on `http://127.0.0.1:11434` or local network host.
+   - At least 1 pulled model (e.g. `llama3.2`, `qwen2.5-coder`, or `smollm2`).
+   - Required for testing zero-egress completions in Enterprise Air-Gap mode.
+
+### 5.2 Isolated Local TLS Container Environment
+1. **Hermetic Test DB & Server:**
+   - Run local application server on test port (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:8080`).
+   - Dedicated mTLS port (default: `8444`) for remote runner WebSocket hub.
+2. **Strict Invariant on Protected Instances:**
+   - **Zero Destructive Actions on `k.hackedyour.info` / `192.168.1.101`:** Do not alter existing provider configurations, reset database state, or delete production runners.
+   - All tests and screenshots must run against local fixtures or strictly non-destructive workspace scopes.
+
+### 5.3 Remote Runner Daemon Test Node
+1. **Non-Root Execution Environment:**
+   - Verify daemon executes as regular user utilizing XDG data directory:
+     `~/.local/share/kanban-runner` (permissions `0o700`).
+2. **Enrollment & Proof-of-Possession:**
+   - Mint single-use token from local server.
+   - Run `echo "<token>" | uv run kanban-agent-runner enroll --server-url https://127.0.0.1:8080 --token-stdin --pool default`.
+   - Start daemon `uv run kanban-agent-runner run` and verify heartbeat shows `online` in `RunnerStudioPage`.
